  "readme": "woscope: oscilloscope emulator This is a POC oscilloscope emulator with live demo Full explanation available on the blag Code is available under MIT license. Example <audio id=\"myAudio\" controls src=\"woscope-music/khrang.m4a\"></audio><br> <canvas id=\"myCanvas\" width=\"800\" height=\"800\"></canvas> <script src=\"dist/woscope.js\"></script> <script> var myCanvas = document.getElementById('myCanvas'), myAudio = document.getElementById('myAudio'); woscope({ canvas: myCanvas, audio: myAudio, callback: function () { myAudio.play(); }, error: function (msg) { console.log('woscope error:', msg); } }); </script> Dev commands npm install # install dev dependencies npm run demo # run demo locally with livereload npm run build # lint and build dist files",
